## Durable Objects

### DO Pattern

```typescript
export class DurableObjectName extends DurableObject {
  private state: DurableObjectState

  constructor(state: DurableObjectState, env: Env) {
    super(state, env)
    this.state = state
  }

  async fetch(request: Request): Promise<Response> {
    const url = new URL(request.url)
    switch (url.pathname) {
      case "/endpoint":
        return this.handleEndpoint(request)
      default:
        return new Response("Not Found", { status: 404 })
    }
  }
}
```

### DO Best Practices

- Use in-memory state with periodic persistence
- Implement atomic operations for critical data
- Use `blockConcurrencyWhile()` for race condition prevention
- Handle errors gracefully with proper HTTP status codes

